k":"laundry","la":39.214124,"lo":9.120825,"d":932,"h":"08:30-13:00,16:30-20:00","ph":"+39 338 8786488"},{"n":"Province of Cagliari","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":39.2192,"lo":9.11722,"d":849,"ds":"The province of Cagliari (Italian: provincia di Cagliari; Sardinian: provìntzia de Casteddu) was a province in the autonomous island region of Sardinia, Italy. Its capital city was Cagliari. It had an area of 4,470 square kilometres (1,730 mi2), and a total population of 543,310 (2001).","wpu":"Province of Cagliari","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Map_Province_of_Cagliari_until_2016.svg/960px-Map_Province_of_Cagliari_until_2016.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Orto Botanico dell'Università di Cagliari","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":39.222,"lo":9.111,"d":893,"ds":"The Orto Botanico dell'Università di Cagliari (5 hectares), also known as the Orto Botanico di Cagliari, is a botanical garden operated by the University of Cagliari and located at Viale S. Ignazio da Laconi 9–11, Cagliari, Sardinia, Italy.","wpu":"Orto Botanico dell'Università di Cagliari","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Orto_Botanico_di_Cagliari.jpg/960px-Orto_Botanico_di_Cagliari.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Torre di San Pancrazio","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":39.221389,"lo":9.117222,"d":1030,"ds":"The Torre di San Pancrazio (in Sardinian language: sa turri de Santu Francau) is a medieval tower in Cagliari, southern Sardinia, Italy. It is located in the Castello historical quarter of the city.","wpu":"Torre di San Pancrazio","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/%2BTour_durch_Cagliari._03.jpg/960px-%2BTour_durch_Cagliari._03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Basilica of San Saturnino","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":39.213889,"lo":9.123333,"d":1148,"ds":"The Basilica of San Saturnino is a Palaeo-Christian church in Cagliari, southern Sardinia, Italy.","wpu":"Basilica of San Saturnino","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Basilica_di_San_Saturnino-Cagliari2.JPG/960px-Basilica_di_San_Saturnino-Cagliari2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Basilica of Our Lady of Bonaria","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":39.208361,"lo":9.125278,"d":1457,"ds":"The Basilica of Our Lady of Bonaria (Italian: Basilica di Nostra Signora di Bonaria) is a Catholic basilica and Marian church located in Cagliari, Italy. The basilica is part of a complex of buildings which make up the Shrine of Our Lady of Bonaria.","wpu":"Basilica of Our Lady of Bonaria","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Basilica_di_Bonaria.JPG/960px-Basilica_di_Bonaria.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Cagliari Courthouse","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":39.216389,"lo":9.126667,"d":1460,"ds":"The Cagliari Courthouse (Italian: Palazzo di Giustizia di Cagliari, lit. 'Palace of Justice of Cagliari') is a judicial complex located in Cagliari, Italy.","wpu":"Cagliari Courthouse","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Palazzo_di_Giustizia_%28Cagliari%29.jpg/960px-Palazzo_di_Giustizia_%28Cagliari%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Teatro Lirico di Cagliari","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":39.225835,"lo":9.123287,"d":1744,"ds":"The Teatro Lirico di Cagliari is an opera house in Cagliari. It is the main theatre of the city. The Teatro Lirico was built in order to provide a large theatre to the city.","wpu":"Teatro Lirico di Cagliari","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d8/Lirico_Cagliari.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Capo Sant'Elia Lighthouse","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":39.184281,"lo":9.147456,"d":4619,"ds":"Capo Sant'Elia Lighthouse (Italian: Faro di Capo Sant'Elia) is an active lighthouse located on Capo Sant'Elia promontory, adjacent to Calamosca Bay which separates the Golfo degli Angeli from that of Quartu Sant'Elena. The structure is situated in the municipality of Quartu Sant'Elena, in the southern Sardinia on the Tyrrhenian Sea.","wpu":"Capo Sant'Elia Lighthouse","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Lighthouse_near_Calamosca.jpg/960px-Lighthouse_near_Calamosca.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Stagno di Cagliari","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":39.2,"lo":9.05,"d":5398,"ds":"The Stagno di Santa Gilla, or Stagno di Cagliari (literally ‘Pool of Cagliari’), is a coastal lagoon at the mouths of the rivers Cixerri and Mannu near Cagliari, on the Golfo degli Angeli in southern Sardinia, Italy. It has been designated as a wetland site of international importance under the Ramsar Convention since 1976 and is ranked among the most important of such areas in the European Union.","wpu":"Stagno di Cagliari","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Stagno_di_cagliari_g1.jpg/960px-Stagno_di_cagliari_g1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Cagliari (, also UK: , US: ; Italian: [ˈkaʎʎari] ; Sardinian: Casteddu [kasˈteɖːu] ; Latin: Caralis [käˈɾaːlɪs]) is a municipality and the capital and largest city of the island of Sardinia, an autonomous region of Italy. It has about 145,981 inhabitants, while its metropolitan city, including 69 other nearby municipalities, has about 536,245 inhabitants. According to Eurostat, the population of the functional urban area, the commuting zone of Cagliari, rises to 476,975.","wpu":"Cagliari","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Cagliari_collage.png/960px-Cagliari_collage.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}